{"id": "EUVD-2026-87237", "enisaUuid": "06a89d7d-b9fc-31e1-b12c-e84723506c88", "description": "RabbitMQ is a messaging and streaming broker. From 4.0.0 until 4.0.22 and 4.1.14 and 4.2.7 and 4.3.1, Atom exhaustion: toatom on global-parameter :name. resourceexists/2 (and the PUT/DELETE handlers) call rabbitdatacoercion:toatom/1 on the :name URL path segment. toatom/1 uses binarytoatom/2 (unsafe). The endpoint requires policymaker (not management, but below A user with the policymaker tag can crash the node by exhausting the atom table via repeated requests to /api/global-parameters/:name with unique :name Management plugin enabled policymaker tag ~1M HTTP. This issue is fixed in versions 4.0.22 and 4.1.14 and 4.2.7 and 4.3.1.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T16:31:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-25T17:48:04", "baseScore": 5.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:H/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/security/advisories/GHSA-q7x8-97rh-cr24", "https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/commit/8fbe6d8112427e85fb9a9206b3eb6e9a3ddd3e39", "https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/commit/fc591e7ee27a29657ca960930acefd3e4217e007", "https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/releases/tag/v4.2.7", "https://github.com/rabbitmq/rabbitmq-server/releases/tag/v4.3.1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-67227"], "assigner": "GitHub_M", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d2dfb72-f1f4-3332-85a9-baae5ad92fad", "product": {"name": "rabbitmq-server", "vendor": {"name": "rabbitmq"}}, "product_version": "4.0.0, < 4.0.22"}, {"id": "9c6dd483-7d51-3606-ab75-f7e5ea2f2295", "product": {"name": "rabbitmq-server", "vendor": {"name": "rabbitmq"}}, "product_version": "4.3.0, < 4.3.1"}, {"id": "9ef3e868-05a3-338d-b45d-6f50358cbc7c", "product": {"name": "rabbitmq-server", "vendor": {"name": "rabbitmq"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0, < 4.2.7"}, {"id": "f2ac6631-690d-348b-80ac-cff5012ac532", "product": {"name": "